    "message": "fix(models): match four more providers to models.dev, and tolerate :free tags\n\nPer-model reasoning capability is keyed by (provider id, model id) against\nmodels.dev, whose provider ids do not always match ours. Four of our\nproviders exist there under a different name and simply had no alias, so\nevery model behind them resolved to unknown and kept today's behaviour\nwhen better data was sitting in the index.\n\nAudited all 56 of our providers against the live 192-provider index.\nCoverage was 40/56; these four take it to 44:\n\n  opencode_go -> opencode-go             26 models\n  wafer       -> wafer.ai                 5 models\n  kimi        -> moonshotai              10 models\n  cloudflare  -> cloudflare-workers-ai   25 models\n\nkimi and cloudflare were resolved from their base URLs rather than name\nsimilarity: KIMI_DEFAULT_BASE is https://api.moonshot.ai/v1, and\nCLOUDFLARE_AI_REST_ROOT is https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4 -- the\nWorkers AI REST root, not the AI Gateway host.\n\nAlso adds a narrow model-id fallback: after an exact match fails, retry\nwithin the SAME provider bucket with a routing/pricing tag stripped, using\nan explicit allow-list of free, nitro and floor. `:thinking` and numeric\ntags are never stripped, because for those the tag IS the reasoning\ndifference -- models.dev carries claude-opus-4-thinking:32000 AND :32768,\nand gemini-2.5-flash-preview:thinking. Conflating them would be wrong in\nexactly the dimension this data configures. An exact hit always beats a\ntag-stripped one, so \"x\" and \"x:free\" keep distinct entries.\n\nThe fallback lives at the lookup layer, not in _normalize_candidates.\nThat helper runs on both the query and the index-building side; widening\nit would make an \"x:free\" row register the bare key \"x\" at build time,\ncolliding with a genuine \"x\" row and destroying the ordering, and would\nleak into the cross-provider-flattened cost/context/vision enrichment\nwhere a bucket boundary does not exist.\n\nSix pairings were considered and REJECTED as different products, recorded\nin-file with reasons so nobody redoes the analysis: llamacpp/llama (Meta's\nhosted API vs a local server), ollama/ollama-cloud, nararoute/orcarouter,\ntokenrouter/openrouter, qwencloud/ebcloud, and mistral_codestral/mistral\n(deferred, different endpoint). Six more have no models.dev entry at all\nand correctly stay unknown: agnes, commandcode, featherless, nous_portal,\nqwencloud_coding, sambanova. A wrong match is strictly worse than none,\nbecause unknown means \"behave exactly as today\".\n\nCross-provider matching by model id alone is deliberately NOT built, and\nthe measurement is recorded: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash appears under 81\nproviders with 16 distinct effort vocabularies and contradictory\ncan_reason values. Reasoning capability is a property of the deployment,\nnot the model.\n\nPROVIDER_ID_ALIASES is a hand-maintained list mirroring another source,\nwhich has always drifted in this project, so a guard now asserts every key\nis a real PROVIDER_CATALOG id, none maps to itself, and none is duplicated\nin the source text.\n\nVerification:\n- Against the real 4 MB index: all four aliases resolve to providers that\n  exist with the expected model counts; kimi/kimi-k3 now reports\n  efforts [high, low, max] and cloudflare's nemotron [high, low, medium];\n  coverage measured at 44/56; all rejected pairings still return None.\n- Mutation-tested: removing an alias, widening the tag allow-list, and\n  reversing the exact-before-stripped order each failed one named test.\n- Full suite on a clean shell: 4758 passed, 6 pre-existing PowerShell\n  installer failures.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty check clean repo-wide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
